  "category": "reversal",
  "note": "\"Press on him his pride\" gets the referent wrong; Sicinius means stress his pride to them.",
  "replacement": "SICINIUS. Let them assemble and, on safer judgment, all revoke your ignorant election. Stress his pride and his old hatred of you. Also, don't forget with what contempt he wore the humble gown, and how he scorned you in his request. But your love, thinking of his services, took from you any grasp of how he was acting then. He did it most mockingly and without dignity, shaped by the old hatred he bears you."
